<title>FRANCE: Pinault Rexel unit buys HTF of Germany.</title>
<headline>Pinault Rexel unit buys HTF of Germany.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pinault-Printemps-Redoute said on Thursday its electrical retailer subsidiary Rexel had signed an agreement to buy 100 percent of HTF of Germany.</p>
<p>The agreement was signed with family shareholders and bankers of HTF, which had 1995 sales of 1.12 billion francs through about 30 shops.</p>
<p>No financial details were given in the Pinault statement.</p>
<p>The acquisition raises Rexel's market share in Germany to around 10 percent from 7.3 percent. Rexel has annual turnover in Germany and Austria of 3.8 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
